<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gohil</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gohil Rajputs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gohil are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> who, according to tradition, entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> from Marwar in the 13th century. Their senior line ruled Bhavnagar State, and junior branches held Palitana, Lathi, Vala and other small Kathiawar states until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a>. Palitana's Gohil rulers controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatrunjaya">Shatrunjaya</a>, one of the holiest Jain pilgrimage sites.</p></div>
